{{-- Definitions every trip-based report shares. Report-specific rules go in the page itself. --}}
<ul>
    <li><strong>On time.</strong> A trip is on time when it left within the cooperative's grace period of the nearest scheduled departure on that route. Early and late are the two sides of that window.</li>
    <li><strong>No timetable.</strong> The route had no timetable when the trip ran, so the trip cannot be judged and is left out of on-time figures. It is not counted as late.</li>
    <li><strong>Unscheduled.</strong> The trip left too far from any scheduled departure to be matched to one. It is also left out of on-time figures.</li>
    <li><strong>Partial data.</strong> Some of the trip's GPS readings were missing (a gap at the start, or too few readings), so distance and speed for that trip are left out or less reliable.</li>
    <li><strong>A dash</strong> means a figure was not measured. It never means zero.</li>
</ul>
